<article class="env-example" id="D42841">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D42841">Example <span data-tag="D42841">5.5.5.6</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a presentable $\infty $-category, and $S$ any collection of morphisms of $\calC $. Then $^{\perp }S$ is saturated; this follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/969C8B" data-tag="969C8B">5.2.8.6</a>. In particular, if $(S_ L, S_ R)$ is a factorization system on $\calC $, then $S_ L$ is saturated. </p>
</article>